{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md'","aggregated_output":"# Investigation and selection\n\nCandidate investigates a sourced question, including unknown requirements, protection premises or legal history. Obligation fixes an applicable responsibility without presuming violation; Check supplies inputs, history and observations. Missing authority calls for contract investigation, missing history for source work or conditional exploration. Neither gap bars a Candidate or licenses an invented obligation.\n\nFirst explain both core relationships from activity_roles and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Follow representative work through owners, qualified support, aggregation, decision, propagation and consumption; explain acquisition, change and loss of context/authority and handling of old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions. Read the supporting membership, history, recovery and completion mechanisms needed for this backbone. Trace callers and callees, important rejection, retry and asynchronous paths; deeper variants may remain open.\n\nSave early discrepancies as sourced Surfaces or specific unknowns even when no obligation is ready. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: unexplained formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks readiness; a usable overview can retain local anomalies. Only a preconfigured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary first; activity_focus does not. A usable map and first Candidate may share a product. Unmapped source work and exploration need no fabricated Fact.\n\nUse behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n\nUse question, counterevidence, unknowns, importance and trigger_rationale to identify what remains unexplained, what existing protection does establish, and what the next action will distinguish. A concise sourced difference suffices; no ranking, mandatory alternative list or confidence threshold. Compare contract reading, smaller exploration and another known relationship before committing to a costly test. “This input has not been run” alone is not a discriminator. An empty unknowns list does not disqualify a check whose earlier investigation established its value.\n\nWhen sourced mechanisms answer the specific suspicion, submit explained and reselect. An unconstructed single obligation may remain unexecuted; this is neither holds nor a budget refund. Fixed artifacts, directed execution tasks, changed premises and open disputes remain visible until explicitly handled. An explicit guard with unresolved ownership, timing, producer or context instead calls for investigation of that premise. A negative result should identify the plausible explanation it excluded and independent premises left open; distinguish it from execution corroborating an already-explained protection. Neither settles the entire Fact or becomes a reason to expand input variants indefinitely. Keep one requirement's independent scenarios together; a genuinely different responsibility gets its own question.\n\nConditional differences with unclear contracts remain exploration or local pause. Once responsibility is grounded, obligation and construction may be separate products. Reuse helpers and legal prefixes only after checking their entry, caller duties, completion order and fault assumptions for this question. A convenient driver must not exclude permitted overlap that supplied the discriminator, nor assume a looser ordering is legal because it produces a difference. Fixed checks must still exercise the investigated premise; a narrower child cannot settle its parent. Use existing F2/F3 when requirement or scope changes. Finish necessary technical repair and review of accepted work; switching questions preserves its debt.\n\nPrioritize consensus safety and explicitly scoped progress duties. Distinguish a sourced numeric/event deadline, implementation-owned automatic continuation without a numeric deadline, and later work explicitly owed by the caller. No numeric deadline does not preclude investigating lost continuation triggers; the word automatic alone supplies no obligation. A possible later event in a comment is not a guarantee that callers produce it. Independently grounded eligibility, accounting, wakeup or correlation duties can be resolved without a client endpoint or global consequence. Shared facts and helpers transfer understanding, not results.\n\nAt natural handoffs retain the answered proposition and remaining discriminator in feedback using tasks/audit.md references. In the next already-needed related map submission, replace the answered original unknown with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete progress reminders. Correct materially misleading higher-level summaries in that same product before reuse; harmless wording differences need no cleanup turn or whole-map sweep. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment, not an understanding label or reference alone. Use behavior-facts.md for primary ownership instead of copying one answer across layers. Source work and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning.\n\nOpen runs continue investigation until controller time/call or actual interruption boundaries. Empty pending_work or disposed registered questions does not exhaust the frontier: use the overview, other consumers/contexts, Surfaces and unread paths. Unit admission exhaustion still permits sourced Candidates, premise investigation and authorized exploration without immediate escalation. Follow each capacity separately; do not repeat handoffs, rerun explained guards, reuse an old Claim for a new proposition or refill budgets. Take a smaller informative step near expiry. Only a preconfigured finite directed task may complete early. Actual cancellation, safety refusal, permission loss and unrecoverable service/tool failure still stop.\n# Conditions, effects and semantic facts\n\nDescribe sourced owners, triggers, guards, state changes, effects and asynchronous boundaries. For a relevant relationship already read, identify who establishes the fact under which conditions and what its consumer actually requires. Include other read establishment, invalidation or reinterpretation paths; unread paths remain unknown or sourced Surfaces.\n\nShared updates do not imply shared follow-up effects. When one entry establishes a fact and schedules a consumer but another only establishes the fact, preserve that distinction in trigger, important_branches, writes, external_effects or async_boundaries. Do not union effects into an unconditional guarantee. Distinguish possible effects, conditional scheduling and guaranteed completion. A Behavior can cover multiple entries when conditions remain clear; split minimally when owners, completion boundaries or meanings cannot be expressed accurately together. Do not enumerate every branch or duplicate a shared Fact.\n\nFact states the assertion actually established for its identity and validity_context, not the strongest effect seen on any path. Reporting, internal accounting, notification and completed external work are distinct. Trace relevant guard inputs to their producer, update point, owner and completion duty instead of trusting a variable name. Conversely, a missing local field is not a missing guarantee when dispatch, admission, serialization or reset supplies it. Assess the composed producer/consumer protection, not each structure in isolation. Absent direct action is a question: inspect alternative consumers, delayed validation, shared scheduling and recovery for the same object and history before alleging a defect.\n\nUse produces_fact_ids/consumes_fact_ids for established relationships needed by later questions; reverse indexes are derived. No name-based edges, mandatory edges, branch fields or completeness scores. Reference validation proves structure, not equivalent path meaning. Guards and observed differences do not supply normative obligations without applicable sources and reasoning.\n\nUse existing map_changes at natural handoffs. Correcting an overstrong abstraction challenges the specific Candidate premise that depended on it; independent results retain their original basis. Use preserves only when requirements, dependencies and observation scope actually remain applicable. Meaning, identity, context and dependency changes cannot masquerade as clarification. No change means no version; keep history and counterevidence.\n\nKeep one primary home for each kind of knowledge: Behavior owns producer conditions, changes, synchronization, notification and exit mechanisms; Fact owns the assertion for its identity and validity_context; Candidate/feedback owns the question's answer, actual execution and remaining discriminator; Activity/core_overview owns the core connections, higher-level understanding and navigation; Surface owns unread entries and reasons; CheckRun/assessment/review owns experiment progress and judgments. Scope owns exclusions. Preserve substantive overviews without copying the same long answer and residuals through every layer. Mapped means association, not resolution. An explained Candidate needs no challenge merely to restate its protection; changed protection or Fact context does require attribution. Use the guide's natural handoff for answered unknowns and tasks/audit.md for Material and execution references.\n# File products for one audit investigation\n\nRead research.json for selected work and shared relationship navigation. A record locator names an existing JSON path, collection and exact match fields; paths are relative to the index directory unless absolute. Select matching records, then read field when present. Historical previews are navigation, not current pending work. Use artifact basis locators and graph_versions for old requirements, not the latest same-ID claim. Materials and execution IDs resolve through records in state.json. Full reviews, drafts and fixed inputs remain at their indexed paths.\n\nWhen capacity permits, supply an optional short Chinese report_title and one to three report_answer sentences in review items, leading with the measured discrepancy and actual observation. State decisive applicability once and keep open disputes visible; leave repeated execution detail and wider exclusions in the scoped records. Keep English semantic reasoning; actual verdicts and measurements prevail. Omission never blocks work or warrants a translation turn.\n\nWrite a complete submission.json using submission.schema.json and product-schemas.json. Cite authorized captured ranges. Follow next_objective and the analysis guide for core_overview readiness; a usable map and first Candidate may share a submission.\n\nWhen repairing a rejected product, set repair_of to its operation_id and submit the whole product. Diagnostics retain ownership: reconsider=submission calls for product repair; reconsider=research_decision requires a different research action, not field repair of an unauthorized stop. Repeated errors may pause only the draft, never unrelated questions.\n\n- continue / pause / explained / obligation: select candidate_id or fork using parent_candidate_id, with a complete current question. Sourced feedback may refine the discriminator before its first obligation; later requirement/scope changes use F2/F3. A fork explains holds/violated/incomplete effects on its parent. Pause supplies resume_conditions; explained cites the protective mechanism. Obligation supplies one attributed claim and source bindings. A complete check may be combined now, or constructed later.\n- check / revise_check: select unit_id (or its Candidate alias), or create an obligation through candidate. Supply plan_path, draft-source harness_path and optional destination-to-draft files; plan.harness.execution_package may select one Go package or Rust crate for this check. Metadata source/files stay empty; the controller fixes executable bytes and adapter support. Never replace target code or dependencies. Revisions name previous_check_id. Driver legality repairs name repair_issue_ids and explain changed inputs and sources; reference every removed conflict's exact issue. Changed executed checker encoding uses encoding_revision. Removing an extra property needs an exact open correspondence issue whose sourced scope/oracle review names out_of_scope_checker_ids; preserve every retained predicate and all harness inputs, then execute and review the explicit successor. Changing the obligation itself still uses F2/F3.\n- research: submit substantive feedback alone with acquired source or retained execution ref_ids, or a complete partial map_path, additive graph_path or scope_path. Feedback alone needs no Candidate or usable overview and creates no map version or Evidence. An identical adjacent pure handoff on unchanged research receives duplicate_of: accepted without new knowledge; continue useful investigation, not rewording. A map may accompany one graph/scope operation. semantic_revision supplies an attributed F2/F3 feedback_path for an existing unit_id and may carry a map. Graph additions cannot invent unowned executable Units.\n- review: select artifact_id; omitted item target_id inherits it. Carries feedback, not a map. Use review_contracts/review_questions: Direct Check requires checker_correspondence; other aspects are optional unless resolving an issue of that aspect. revision_needed names challenged_components. Resolve exact issue_ids using acquired Material source_ids, a concise answer and retained evidence_ids when relevant. For supplied conditions, use condition_dispositions with exact condition_id, sources and applicability; current_judgment remains unresolved. Unchanged sources and reasoning can be referenced, not recopied. The review guide defines semantic criteria. Candidate applicability review creates no execution Evidence.\n- explore: submit a question, draft-source harness_path, optional files and optional execution_package with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package. Clean-copy output guides construction without property Evidence.\n- stop: candidate/family/focus release local work; unfinished Units and disputes remain. A local tool/resource gap supplies resume_conditions. Focus releases unfinished research while preserving explained/closed/paused dispositions and each question's own conditions; shared focus reasons stay in this stop record. Open runs reject scope=run: continue with research, exploration or another Candidate within remaining authorization. Only a preconfigured finite directed_question may end with run/bounded_completed after its task is disposed; cite the explained, closed or checked Candidate. Cancellation, permission/service failure and exhausted time/calls are controller events, never submission authority.\n\nFor Go, omit execution_package to retain the run default package and main-file destination. An explicit local directory selects that package and places the primary file there using the configured basename. Helpers in files remain relative to the workspace root. The controller fixes the effective package and bytes before execution; it runs Go directly in a clean copy, without a root launcher. Select only one existing package in the captured module; paths, patterns, nested modules, workspaces and dependency overrides cannot expand authorization. Python does not support this override.\n\nFor Rust, execution_package selects one captured crate directory and tests/<configured basename>.rs, with workspace-relative helpers. Use research.build_inputs (fixed lock, tools, metadata and selected-test compilation) to check available APIs against effective features; a source declaration alone does not establish active cfg or public reachability. Original manifests and dev-dependencies determine features; no extra flags are added. Omit logging or helper initialization unrelated to the discriminator. The backend instructions describe private seed reuse and current harness execution; preparation consumes the run deadline and supplies no observations. Never replace manifests, locks, build scripts or tool configuration.\n\nA formal question names one principal fact_ids entry, lifecycle, direct behavior_ids, sourced A1/A2 relationship, contexts, event_paths, importance and trigger_rationale. supporting_behavior_ids maps distinct Behavior IDs to their causal role. audit_spec_version may be omitted for the current basis. A map file's version is its accepted base (1 initially); the controller assigns resulting versions, including questions in combined products and F2/F3 patches. Do not guess current+1. Unchanged Candidates retain their historical basis. A supporting-layer question cites its actual consumer or core relationship and declares the supported A1/A2 activity; a local storage obligation need not become a whole-cluster consequence. If that relationship lacks sources, investigate or retain feedback instead of inventing a core label.\n\nThe controller derives actual map differences and reverse indexes. map_changes explains modified/removed objects and new producers or consumers of an existing principal Fact, with impact (clarification/meaning/dependency), acquired source_ids and rationale. Use one preserves explanation for unchanged requirements, dependencies and observation scope, or challenges mapping saved Candidate IDs to specific disputed premises. A corrected principal Fact requires a challenge; clarification cannot disguise identity/context/edge changes or removal. Independent additions need no invented revision and may still challenge a prior interpretation.\n\nCoherent knowledge and its issues are accepted together; unaffected checks retain their basis. reconnect_questions updates explicitly selected questions. ScopeUpdate/F3 expands dependencies under its existing write rules; changed normative or fault/configuration applicability uses F2. No-op maps create no version.\n\nFor every feedback shape, including one accompanying a map, Candidate or review, ref_ids directly includes each saved CheckRun whose execution it explains, alongside relevant Candidate, Behavior, Fact, surface:<entry_point> and Material IDs. Obtain execution IDs from research.json.explorations[*].executions[*].check_id or the exact records locator, not operation/plan IDs or prose. Explaining only a repaired execution references only that run; a joint explanation references both failure and repair and distinguishes their observations. Shared sources, Behavior or harness names do not associate executions. Source-only answers need no execution reference. Map/map_changes source_ids remain Material references. understanding records learning, not a map change; use the guide's natural handoff. question_updates revises Candidate unknowns/resume_conditions with sources, retaining requirements and counterevidence. Historical remaining is then-remaining; current execution/review records remain authoritative.\n\nClaim/Scope owns requirement and applicability; Harness legality records this history and caller duties. Use the experiments reference for predicate correspondence, observation synchronization, prerequisite waits and cleanup responsibility during construction and review. Unreached setup retains its observation and calls for minimal repair preserving the discriminator. claim.concern classifies responsibility, not confidence.\n\nOptional preflight: run validation.command followed by the draft-relative filename in an existing Codex tool call. It shares acceptance preparation, writes no accepted state and executes no target; formal submission rechecks fixed bytes and current state without a preflight ticket or reserved budget. research.json capacity and preflight elapsed_seconds describe saved run checkpoints, not live time within this turn. Use the controller's current turn allocation and referenced CheckRun for the actual time basis; its estimated UTC deadline is explanatory and the runner enforces the hard timeout. new_obligation is an entry capability, not a complete check/review budget; remaining.agent_calls counts future turns, not local work in this running turn.\n\nOnce a sourced product independently expresses substantive research progress, you may return it and continue in the next turn. Initial delivery need not wait for a Candidate, obligation, harness or all local trials. Before the two-line overview and its connection are usable, retain real partial understanding through research feedback or a partial map; do not claim full readiness. Combine products when ready. Passing preflight does not force immediate submission, but further expansion should serve a concrete new discriminator within the remaining turn time. A feedback-only exploration answer retains conditions, observations and open responsibility/history/endpoint questions under the same reference rule. Keep rejected larger drafts and diagnostics separate; the small product neither repairs nor partially accepts them. There is no required first-turn product, separate feedback turn or delivery quota. A reliable completion receipt fixes only declared product files before deadline handling; saved bytes are not acceptance or Evidence. Without that receipt, drafts remain unsubmitted. Natural expiry needs no closing submission.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
