{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/ballot_leader_election.rs | head -420; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/omni_paxos.rs | head -360'","aggregated_output":"     1\tuse std::cmp::Ordering;\n     2\t\n     3\t/// Ballot Leader Election algorithm for electing new leaders\n     4\tuse crate::{\n     5\t    sequence_paxos::{Phase, Role},\n     6\t    util::{defaults::*, ConfigurationId, FlexibleQuorum, Quorum},\n     7\t};\n     8\t\n     9\t#[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    10\tuse crate::utils::logger::create_logger;\n    11\tuse crate::{\n    12\t    messages::ballot_leader_election::{\n    13\t        BLEMessage, HeartbeatMsg, HeartbeatReply, HeartbeatRequest,\n    14\t    },\n    15\t    util::NodeId,\n    16\t    OmniPaxosConfig,\n    17\t};\n    18\t#[cfg(feature = \"serde\")]\n    19\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n    20\t#[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    21\tuse slog::{info, trace, Logger};\n    22\t\n    23\t/// Used to define a Sequence Paxos epoch\n    24\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Eq, Debug, Default, PartialEq)]\n    25\t#[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n    26\tpub struct Ballot {\n    27\t    /// The identifier for the configuration that the replica with this ballot is part of.\n    28\t    pub config_id: ConfigurationId,\n    29\t    /// Ballot number\n    30\t    pub n: u32,\n    31\t    /// Custom priority parameter\n    32\t    pub priority: u32,\n    33\t    /// The pid of the process\n    34\t    pub pid: NodeId,\n    35\t}\n    36\t\n    37\timpl Ballot {\n    38\t    /// Creates a new Ballot\n    39\t    /// # Arguments\n    40\t    /// * `config_id` - The identifier for the configuration that the replica with this ballot is part of.\n    41\t    /// * `n` - Ballot number.\n    42\t    /// * `pid` -  Used as tiebreaker for total ordering of ballots.\n    43\t    pub fn with(config_id: ConfigurationId, n: u32, priority: u32, pid: NodeId) -> Ballot {\n    44\t        Ballot {\n    45\t            config_id,\n    46\t            n,\n    47\t            priority,\n    48\t            pid,\n    49\t        }\n    50\t    }\n    51\t}\n    52\t\n    53\timpl Ord for Ballot {\n    54\t    fn cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Ordering {\n    55\t        (self.n, self.priority, self.pid).cmp(&(other.n, other.priority, other.pid))\n    56\t    }\n    57\t}\n    58\t\n    59\timpl PartialOrd for Ballot {\n    60\t    fn partial_cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Option<Ordering> {\n    61\t        Some(self.cmp(other))\n    62\t    }\n    63\t}\n    64\t\n    65\tconst INITIAL_ROUND: u32 = 1;\n    66\tconst RECOVERY_ROUND: u32 = 0;\n    67\t\n    68\t/// A Ballot Leader Election component. Used in conjunction with OmniPaxos to handle the election of a leader for a cluster of OmniPaxos servers,\n    69\t/// incoming messages and produces outgoing messages that the user has to fetch periodically and send using a network implementation.\n    70\t/// User also has to periodically fetch the decided entries that are guaranteed to be strongly consistent and linearizable, and therefore also safe to be used in the higher level application.\n    71\tpub(crate) struct BallotLeaderElection {\n    72\t    /// The identifier for the configuration that this instance is part of.\n    73\t    configuration_id: ConfigurationId,\n    74\t    /// Process identifier used to uniquely identify this instance.\n    75\t    pid: NodeId,\n    76\t    /// Vector that holds the pids of all the other servers.\n    77\t    peers: Vec<NodeId>,\n    78\t    /// The current round of the heartbeat cycle.\n    79\t    hb_round: u32,\n    80\t    /// The heartbeat replies this instance received during the current round.\n    81\t    heartbeat_replies: Vec<HeartbeatReply>,\n    82\t    /// Vector that holds all the received heartbeats from the previous heartbeat round, including the current node. Only used to display the connectivity of this node in the UI.\n    83\t    /// Represents nodes that are currently alive from the view of the current node.\n    84\t    prev_replies: Vec<HeartbeatReply>,\n    85\t    /// Holds the current ballot of this instance.\n    86\t    current_ballot: Ballot,\n    87\t    /// The current leader of this instance.\n    88\t    leader: Ballot,\n    89\t    /// A happy node either sees that it is, is connected to, or sees evidence of a potential leader\n    90\t    /// for the cluster. If a node is unhappy then it is seeking a new leader.\n    91\t    happy: bool,\n    92\t    /// The number of replicas inside the cluster whose heartbeats are needed to become and remain the leader.\n    93\t    quorum: Quorum,\n    94\t    /// Vector which holds all the outgoing messages of the BLE instance.\n    95\t    outgoing: Vec<BLEMessage>,\n    96\t    /// Logger used to output the status of the component.\n    97\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    98\t    logger: Logger,\n    99\t}\n   100\t\n   101\timpl BallotLeaderElection {\n   102\t    /// Construct a new BallotLeaderElection node\n   103\t    pub(crate) fn with(config: BLEConfig, recovered_leader: Option<Ballot>) -> Self {\n   104\t        let config_id = config.configuration_id;\n   105\t        let pid = config.pid;\n   106\t        let peers = config.peers;\n   107\t        let num_nodes = &peers.len() + 1;\n   108\t        let quorum = Quorum::with(config.flexible_quorum, num_nodes);\n   109\t        let mut initial_ballot = Ballot::with(config_id, INITIAL_ROUND, config.priority, pid);\n   110\t        let initial_leader = match recovered_leader {\n   111\t            Some(b) if b != Ballot::default() => {\n   112\t                // Prevents a recovered server from retaining BLE leadership with the same ballot.\n   113\t                initial_ballot.n = RECOVERY_ROUND;\n   114\t                b\n   115\t            }\n   116\t            _ => initial_ballot,\n   117\t        };\n   118\t        let mut ble = BallotLeaderElection {\n   119\t            configuration_id: config_id,\n   120\t            pid,\n   121\t            peers,\n   122\t            hb_round: 0,\n   123\t            heartbeat_replies: Vec::with_capacity(num_nodes),\n   124\t            prev_replies: Vec::with_capacity(num_nodes),\n   125\t            current_ballot: initial_ballot,\n   126\t            leader: initial_leader,\n   127\t            happy: true,\n   128\t            quorum,\n   129\t            outgoing: Vec::with_capacity(config.buffer_size),\n   130\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   131\t            logger: {\n   132\t                if let Some(logger) = config.custom_logger {\n   133\t                    logger\n   134\t                } else {\n   135\t                    let s = config\n   136\t                        .logger_file_path\n   137\t                        .unwrap_or_else(|| format!(\"logs/paxos_{}.log\", pid));\n   138\t                    create_logger(s.as_str())\n   139\t                }\n   140\t            },\n   141\t        };\n   142\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   143\t        {\n   144\t            info!(\n   145\t                ble.logger,\n   146\t                \"Ballot Leader Election component pid: {} created!\", pid\n   147\t            );\n   148\t        }\n   149\t        ble.new_hb_round();\n   150\t        ble\n   151\t    }\n   152\t\n   153\t    /// Update the custom priority used in the Ballot for this server. Note that changing the\n   154\t    /// priority triggers a leader re-election.\n   155\t    pub(crate) fn set_priority(&mut self, p: u32) {\n   156\t        self.current_ballot.priority = p;\n   157\t    }\n   158\t\n   159\t    /// Returns reference to outgoing messages\n   160\t    pub(crate) fn outgoing_mut(&mut self) -> &mut Vec<BLEMessage> {\n   161\t        &mut self.outgoing\n   162\t    }\n   163\t\n   164\t    /// Handle an incoming message.\n   165\t    /// # Arguments\n   166\t    /// * `m` - the message to be handled.\n   167\t    pub(crate) fn handle(&mut self, m: BLEMessage) {\n   168\t        match m.msg {\n   169\t            HeartbeatMsg::Request(req) => self.handle_request(m.from, req),\n   170\t            HeartbeatMsg::Reply(rep) => self.handle_reply(rep),\n   171\t        }\n   172\t    }\n   173\t\n   174\t    /// Initiates a new heartbeat round.\n   175\t    pub(crate) fn new_hb_round(&mut self) {\n   176\t        self.prev_replies = std::mem::take(&mut self.heartbeat_replies);\n   177\t        self.hb_round += 1;\n   178\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   179\t        trace!(\n   180\t            self.logger,\n   181\t            \"Initiate new heartbeat round: {}\",\n   182\t            self.hb_round\n   183\t        );\n   184\t        for peer in &self.peers {\n   185\t            let hb_request = HeartbeatRequest {\n   186\t                round: self.hb_round,\n   187\t            };\n   188\t            self.outgoing.push(BLEMessage {\n   189\t                from: self.pid,\n   190\t                to: *peer,\n   191\t                msg: HeartbeatMsg::Request(hb_request),\n   192\t            });\n   193\t        }\n   194\t    }\n   195\t\n   196\t    /// End of a heartbeat round. Returns current leader and election status.\n   197\t    pub(crate) fn hb_timeout(\n   198\t        &mut self,\n   199\t        seq_paxos_state: &(Role, Phase),\n   200\t        seq_paxos_promise: Ballot,\n   201\t    ) -> Option<Ballot> {\n   202\t        self.update_leader();\n   203\t        self.update_happiness(seq_paxos_state);\n   204\t        self.check_takeover();\n   205\t        self.new_hb_round();\n   206\t        if seq_paxos_promise > self.leader {\n   207\t            // Sync leader with Paxos promise in case ballot didn't make it to BLE followers\n   208\t            // or become_leader() was called.\n   209\t            self.leader = seq_paxos_promise;\n   210\t            if seq_paxos_promise.pid == self.pid {\n   211\t                self.current_ballot = seq_paxos_promise;\n   212\t            }\n   213\t            self.happy = true;\n   214\t        }\n   215\t        if self.leader == self.current_ballot {\n   216\t            Some(self.current_ballot)\n   217\t        } else {\n   218\t            None\n   219\t        }\n   220\t    }\n   221\t\n   222\t    fn update_leader(&mut self) {\n   223\t        let max_reply_ballot = self.heartbeat_replies.iter().map(|r| r.ballot).max();\n   224\t        if let Some(max) = max_reply_ballot {\n   225\t            if max > self.leader {\n   226\t                self.leader = max;\n   227\t            }\n   228\t        }\n   229\t    }\n   230\t\n   231\t    fn update_happiness(&mut self, seq_paxos_state: &(Role, Phase)) {\n   232\t        self.happy = if self.leader == self.current_ballot {\n   233\t            let potential_followers = self\n   234\t                .heartbeat_replies\n   235\t                .iter()\n   236\t                .filter(|hb_reply| hb_reply.leader <= self.current_ballot)\n   237\t                .count();\n   238\t            let can_form_quorum = match seq_paxos_state {\n   239\t                (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) => {\n   240\t                    self.quorum.is_accept_quorum(potential_followers + 1)\n   241\t                }\n   242\t                _ => self.quorum.is_prepare_quorum(potential_followers + 1),\n   243\t            };\n   244\t            if can_form_quorum {\n   245\t                true\n   246\t            } else {\n   247\t                let see_larger_happy_leader = self\n   248\t                    .heartbeat_replies\n   249\t                    .iter()\n   250\t                    .any(|r| r.leader > self.current_ballot && r.happy);\n   251\t                see_larger_happy_leader\n   252\t            }\n   253\t        } else {\n   254\t            self.heartbeat_replies\n   255\t                .iter()\n   256\t                .any(|r| r.ballot == self.leader && r.happy)\n   257\t        };\n   258\t    }\n   259\t\n   260\t    fn check_takeover(&mut self) {\n   261\t        if !self.happy {\n   262\t            let all_neighbors_unhappy = self.heartbeat_replies.iter().all(|r| !r.happy);\n   263\t            let im_quorum_connected = self\n   264\t                .quorum\n   265\t                .is_prepare_quorum(self.heartbeat_replies.len() + 1);\n   266\t            if all_neighbors_unhappy && im_quorum_connected {\n   267\t                // We increment past our leader instead of max of unhappy ballots because we\n   268\t                // assume we have already checked leader for this round so they should be equal\n   269\t                self.current_ballot.n = self.leader.n + 1;\n   270\t                self.leader = self.current_ballot;\n   271\t                self.happy = true;\n   272\t            }\n   273\t        }\n   274\t    }\n   275\t\n   276\t    fn handle_request(&mut self, from: NodeId, req: HeartbeatRequest) {\n   277\t        let hb_reply = HeartbeatReply {\n   278\t            round: req.round,\n   279\t            ballot: self.current_ballot,\n   280\t            leader: self.leader,\n   281\t            happy: self.happy,\n   282\t        };\n   283\t        self.outgoing.push(BLEMessage {\n   284\t            from: self.pid,\n   285\t            to: from,\n   286\t            msg: HeartbeatMsg::Reply(hb_reply),\n   287\t        });\n   288\t    }\n   289\t\n   290\t    fn handle_reply(&mut self, rep: HeartbeatReply) {\n   291\t        if rep.round == self.hb_round && rep.ballot.config_id == self.configuration_id {\n   292\t            self.heartbeat_replies.push(rep);\n   293\t        }\n   294\t    }\n   295\t\n   296\t    pub(crate) fn get_current_ballot(&self) -> Ballot {\n   297\t        self.current_ballot\n   298\t    }\n   299\t\n   300\t    pub(crate) fn get_ballots(&self) -> Vec<HeartbeatReply> {\n   301\t        self.prev_replies.clone()\n   302\t    }\n   303\t}\n   304\t\n   305\t/// Configuration for `BallotLeaderElection`.\n   306\t/// # Fields\n   307\t/// * `configuration_id`: The identifier for the configuration that this node is part of.\n   308\t/// * `pid`: The unique identifier of this node. Must not be 0.\n   309\t/// * `peers`: The peers of this node i.e. the `pid`s of the other servers in the configuration.\n   310\t/// * `priority`: Set custom priority for this node to be elected as the leader.\n   311\t/// * `flexible_quorum` : Defines read and write quorum sizes. Can be used for different latency vs fault tolerance tradeoffs.\n   312\t/// * `buffer_size`: The buffer size for outgoing messages.\n   313\t/// * `logger_file_path`: The path where the default logger logs events.\n   314\t#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n   315\tpub(crate) struct BLEConfig {\n   316\t    configuration_id: ConfigurationId,\n   317\t    pid: NodeId,\n   318\t    peers: Vec<NodeId>,\n   319\t    priority: u32,\n   320\t    flexible_quorum: Option<FlexibleQuorum>,\n   321\t    buffer_size: usize,\n   322\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   323\t    logger_file_path: Option<String>,\n   324\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   325\t    custom_logger: Option<Logger>,\n   326\t}\n   327\t\n   328\timpl From<OmniPaxosConfig> for BLEConfig {\n   329\t    fn from(config: OmniPaxosConfig) -> Self {\n   330\t        let pid = config.server_config.pid;\n   331\t        let peers = config\n   332\t            .cluster_config\n   333\t            .nodes\n   334\t            .into_iter()\n   335\t            .filter(|x| *x != pid)\n   336\t            .collect();\n   337\t\n   338\t        Self {\n   339\t            configuration_id: config.cluster_config.configuration_id,\n   340\t            pid,\n   341\t            peers,\n   342\t            priority: config.server_config.leader_priority,\n   343\t            flexible_quorum: config.cluster_config.flexible_quorum,\n   344\t            buffer_size: BLE_BUFFER_SIZE,\n   345\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   346\t            logger_file_path: config.server_config.logger_file_path,\n   347\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   348\t            custom_logger: config.server_config.custom_logger,\n   349\t        }\n   350\t    }\n   351\t}\n     1\tuse crate::{\n     2\t    ballot_leader_election::{Ballot, BallotLeaderElection},\n     3\t    errors::{valid_config, ConfigError},\n     4\t    messages::Message,\n     5\t    sequence_paxos::{Phase, SequencePaxos},\n     6\t    storage::{Entry, StopSign, Storage},\n     7\t    util::{\n     8\t        defaults::{BUFFER_SIZE, ELECTION_TIMEOUT, FLUSH_BATCH_TIMEOUT, RESEND_MESSAGE_TIMEOUT},\n     9\t        ConfigurationId, FlexibleQuorum, LogEntry, LogicalClock, NodeId,\n    10\t    },\n    11\t    utils::{ui, ui::ClusterState},\n    12\t};\n    13\t#[cfg(any(feature = \"toml_config\", feature = \"serde\"))]\n    14\tuse serde::Deserialize;\n    15\t#[cfg(feature = \"serde\")]\n    16\tuse serde::Serialize;\n    17\t#[cfg(feature = \"toml_config\")]\n    18\tuse std::fs;\n    19\tuse std::{\n    20\t    error::Error,\n    21\t    fmt::{Debug, Display},\n    22\t    ops::RangeBounds,\n    23\t};\n    24\t#[cfg(feature = \"toml_config\")]\n    25\tuse toml;\n    26\t\n    27\t/// Configuration for `OmniPaxos`.\n    28\t/// # Fields\n    29\t/// * `cluster_config`: The configuration settings that are cluster-wide.\n    30\t/// * `server_config`: The configuration settings that are specific to this OmniPaxos server.\n    31\t#[allow(missing_docs)]\n    32\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]\n    33\t#[cfg_attr(feature = \"toml_config\", derive(Deserialize), serde(default))]\n    34\tpub struct OmniPaxosConfig {\n    35\t    pub cluster_config: ClusterConfig,\n    36\t    pub server_config: ServerConfig,\n    37\t}\n    38\t\n    39\timpl OmniPaxosConfig {\n    40\t    /// Checks that all the fields of the cluster config are valid.\n    41\t    pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), ConfigError> {\n    42\t        self.cluster_config.validate()?;\n    43\t        self.server_config.validate()?;\n    44\t        valid_config!(\n    45\t            self.cluster_config.nodes.contains(&self.server_config.pid),\n    46\t            \"Nodes must include own server pid\"\n    47\t        );\n    48\t        Ok(())\n    49\t    }\n    50\t\n    51\t    /// Creates a new `OmniPaxosConfig` from a `toml` file.\n    52\t    #[cfg(feature = \"toml_config\")]\n    53\t    pub fn with_toml(file_path: &str) -> Result<Self, ConfigError> {\n    54\t        let config_file = fs::read_to_string(file_path)?;\n    55\t        let config: OmniPaxosConfig = toml::from_str(&config_file)?;\n    56\t        config.validate()?;\n    57\t        Ok(config)\n    58\t    }\n    59\t\n    60\t    /// Checks all configuration fields and returns the local OmniPaxos node if successful.\n    61\t    pub fn build<T, B>(self, storage: B) -> Result<OmniPaxos<T, B>, ConfigError>\n    62\t    where\n    63\t        T: Entry,\n    64\t        B: Storage<T>,\n    65\t    {\n    66\t        self.validate()?;\n    67\t        // Use stored ballot as initial BLE leader\n    68\t        let recovered_leader = storage\n    69\t            .get_promise()\n    70\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read promise\");\n    71\t        Ok(OmniPaxos {\n    72\t            ble: BallotLeaderElection::with(self.clone().into(), recovered_leader),\n    73\t            election_clock: LogicalClock::with(self.server_config.election_tick_timeout),\n    74\t            resend_message_clock: LogicalClock::with(\n    75\t                self.server_config.resend_message_tick_timeout,\n    76\t            ),\n    77\t            flush_batch_clock: LogicalClock::with(self.server_config.flush_batch_tick_timeout),\n    78\t            seq_paxos: SequencePaxos::with(self.into(), storage),\n    79\t        })\n    80\t    }\n    81\t}\n    82\t\n    83\t/// Configuration for an `OmniPaxos` cluster.\n    84\t/// # Fields\n    85\t/// * `configuration_id`: The identifier for the cluster configuration that this OmniPaxos server is part of.\n    86\t/// * `nodes`: The nodes in the cluster i.e. the `pid`s of the other servers in the configuration.\n    87\t/// * `flexible_quorum` : Defines read and write quorum sizes. Can be used for different latency vs fault tolerance tradeoffs.\n    88\t#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Default)]\n    89\t#[cfg_attr(any(feature = \"serde\", feature = \"toml_config\"), derive(Deserialize))]\n    90\t#[cfg_attr(feature = \"toml_config\", serde(default))]\n    91\t#[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize))]\n    92\tpub struct ClusterConfig {\n    93\t    /// The identifier for the cluster configuration that this OmniPaxos server is part of. Must\n    94\t    /// not be 0 and be greater than the previous configuration's id.\n    95\t    pub configuration_id: ConfigurationId,\n    96\t    /// The nodes in the cluster i.e. the `pid`s of the servers in the configuration.\n    97\t    pub nodes: Vec<NodeId>,\n    98\t    /// Defines read and write quorum sizes. Can be used for different latency vs fault tolerance tradeoffs.\n    99\t    pub flexible_quorum: Option<FlexibleQuorum>,\n   100\t}\n   101\t\n   102\timpl ClusterConfig {\n   103\t    /// Checks that all the fields of the cluster config are valid.\n   104\t    pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), ConfigError> {\n   105\t        let num_nodes = self.nodes.len();\n   106\t        valid_config!(num_nodes > 1, \"Need more than 1 node\");\n   107\t        valid_config!(self.configuration_id != 0, \"Configuration ID cannot be 0\");\n   108\t        if let Some(FlexibleQuorum {\n   109\t            read_quorum_size,\n   110\t            write_quorum_size,\n   111\t        }) = self.flexible_quorum\n   112\t        {\n   113\t            valid_config!(\n   114\t                read_quorum_size + write_quorum_size > num_nodes,\n   115\t                \"The quorums must overlap i.e., the sum of their sizes must exceed the # of nodes\"\n   116\t            );\n   117\t            valid_config!(\n   118\t                read_quorum_size >= 2 && read_quorum_size <= num_nodes,\n   119\t                \"Read quorum must be in range 2 to # of nodes in the cluster\"\n   120\t            );\n   121\t            valid_config!(\n   122\t                write_quorum_size >= 2 && write_quorum_size <= num_nodes,\n   123\t                \"Write quorum must be in range 2 to # of nodes in the cluster\"\n   124\t            );\n   125\t            valid_config!(\n   126\t                read_quorum_size >= write_quorum_size,\n   127\t                \"Read quorum size must be >= the write quorum size.\"\n   128\t            );\n   129\t        }\n   130\t        Ok(())\n   131\t    }\n   132\t\n   133\t    /// Checks all configuration fields and builds a local OmniPaxos node with settings for this\n   134\t    /// node defined in `server_config` and using storage `with_storage`.\n   135\t    pub fn build_for_server<T, B>(\n   136\t        self,\n   137\t        server_config: ServerConfig,\n   138\t        with_storage: B,\n   139\t    ) -> Result<OmniPaxos<T, B>, ConfigError>\n   140\t    where\n   141\t        T: Entry,\n   142\t        B: Storage<T>,\n   143\t    {\n   144\t        let op_config = OmniPaxosConfig {\n   145\t            cluster_config: self,\n   146\t            server_config,\n   147\t        };\n   148\t        op_config.build(with_storage)\n   149\t    }\n   150\t}\n   151\t\n   152\t/// Configuration for a singular `OmniPaxos` instance in a cluster.\n   153\t/// # Fields\n   154\t/// * `pid`: The unique identifier of this node. Must not be 0.\n   155\t/// * `election_tick_timeout`: The number of calls to `tick()` before leader election is updated. If this is set to 5 and `tick()` is called every 10ms, then the election timeout will be 50ms. Must not be 0.\n   156\t/// * `resend_message_tick_timeout`: The number of calls to `tick()` before a message is considered dropped and thus resent. Must not be 0.\n   157\t/// * `buffer_size`: The buffer size for outgoing messages.\n   158\t/// * `batch_size`: The size of the buffer for log batching. The default is 1, which means no batching.\n   159\t/// * `logger_file_path`: The path where the default logger logs events.\n   160\t/// * `leader_priority` : Custom priority for this node to be elected as the leader.\n   161\t#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n   162\t#[cfg_attr(feature = \"toml_config\", derive(Deserialize), serde(default))]\n   163\tpub struct ServerConfig {\n   164\t    /// The unique identifier of this node. Must not be 0.\n   165\t    pub pid: NodeId,\n   166\t    /// The number of calls to `tick()` before leader election is updated. If this is set to 5 and `tick()` is called every 10ms, then the election timeout will be 50ms.\n   167\t    pub election_tick_timeout: u64,\n   168\t    /// The number of calls to `tick()` before a message is considered dropped and thus resent. Must not be 0.\n   169\t    pub resend_message_tick_timeout: u64,\n   170\t    /// The buffer size for outgoing messages.\n   171\t    pub buffer_size: usize,\n   172\t    /// The size of the buffer for log batching. The default is 1, which means no batching.\n   173\t    pub batch_size: usize,\n   174\t    /// The number of calls to `tick()` before the batched log entries are flushed.\n   175\t    pub flush_batch_tick_timeout: u64,\n   176\t    /// Custom priority for this node to be elected as the leader.\n   177\t    pub leader_priority: u32,\n   178\t    /// The path where the default logger logs events.\n   179\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   180\t    pub logger_file_path: Option<String>,\n   181\t    /// Custom logger, if provided, will be used instead of the default logger.\n   182\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   183\t    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"toml_config\", serde(skip_deserializing))]\n   184\t    pub custom_logger: Option<slog::Logger>,\n   185\t}\n   186\t\n   187\timpl ServerConfig {\n   188\t    /// Checks that all the fields of the server config are valid.\n   189\t    pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), ConfigError> {\n   190\t        valid_config!(self.pid != 0, \"Server pid cannot be 0\");\n   191\t        valid_config!(self.buffer_size != 0, \"Buffer size must be greater than 0\");\n   192\t        valid_config!(self.batch_size != 0, \"Batch size must be greater than 0\");\n   193\t        valid_config!(\n   194\t            self.election_tick_timeout != 0,\n   195\t            \"Election tick timeout must be greater than 0\"\n   196\t        );\n   197\t        valid_config!(\n   198\t            self.resend_message_tick_timeout != 0,\n   199\t            \"Resend message tick timeout must be greater than 0\"\n   200\t        );\n   201\t        Ok(())\n   202\t    }\n   203\t}\n   204\t\n   205\timpl Default for ServerConfig {\n   206\t    fn default() -> Self {\n   207\t        Self {\n   208\t            pid: 0,\n   209\t            election_tick_timeout: ELECTION_TIMEOUT,\n   210\t            resend_message_tick_timeout: RESEND_MESSAGE_TIMEOUT,\n   211\t            buffer_size: BUFFER_SIZE,\n   212\t            batch_size: 1,\n   213\t            flush_batch_tick_timeout: FLUSH_BATCH_TIMEOUT,\n   214\t            leader_priority: 0,\n   215\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   216\t            logger_file_path: None,\n   217\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   218\t            custom_logger: None,\n   219\t        }\n   220\t    }\n   221\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t/// The `OmniPaxos` struct represents an OmniPaxos server. Maintains the replicated log that can be read from and appended to.\n   224\t/// It also handles incoming messages and produces outgoing messages that you need to fetch and send periodically using your own network implementation.\n   225\tpub struct OmniPaxos<T, B>\n   226\twhere\n   227\t    T: Entry,\n   228\t    B: Storage<T>,\n   229\t{\n   230\t    seq_paxos: SequencePaxos<T, B>,\n   231\t    ble: BallotLeaderElection,\n   232\t    election_clock: LogicalClock,\n   233\t    resend_message_clock: LogicalClock,\n   234\t    flush_batch_clock: LogicalClock,\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\timpl<T, B> OmniPaxos<T, B>\n   238\twhere\n   239\t    T: Entry,\n   240\t    B: Storage<T>,\n   241\t{\n   242\t    /// Initiates the trim process.\n   243\t    /// # Arguments\n   244\t    /// * `trim_index` - Deletes all entries up to [`trim_index`], if the [`trim_index`] is `None` then the minimum index accepted by **ALL** servers will be used as the [`trim_index`].\n   245\t    pub fn trim(&mut self, trim_index: Option<usize>) -> Result<(), CompactionErr> {\n   246\t        self.seq_paxos.trim(trim_index)\n   247\t    }\n   248\t\n   249\t    /// Trim the log and create a snapshot. ** Note: only up to the `decided_idx` can be snapshotted **\n   250\t    /// # Arguments\n   251\t    /// `compact_idx` - Snapshots all entries < [`compact_idx`], if the [`compact_idx`] is None then the decided index will be used.\n   252\t    /// `local_only` - If `true`, only this server snapshots the log. If `false` all servers performs the snapshot.\n   253\t    pub fn snapshot(\n   254\t        &mut self,\n   255\t        compact_idx: Option<usize>,\n   256\t        local_only: bool,\n   257\t    ) -> Result<(), CompactionErr> {\n   258\t        self.seq_paxos.snapshot(compact_idx, local_only)\n   259\t    }\n   260\t\n   261\t    /// Return the decided index. 0 means that no entry has been decided.\n   262\t    pub fn get_decided_idx(&self) -> usize {\n   263\t        self.seq_paxos.get_decided_idx()\n   264\t    }\n   265\t\n   266\t    /// Return the accepted index of this node's log (as if it was never compacted).\n   267\t    /// Equal to the index of the last accepted entry; useful for tagging a just-appended\n   268\t    /// entry so that decision can be awaited.\n   269\t    pub fn get_accepted_idx(&self) -> usize {\n   270\t        self.seq_paxos.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx()\n   271\t    }\n   272\t\n   273\t    /// Return the number of entries currently buffered for batching (see\n   274\t    /// `ServerConfig::batch_size`), not yet reflected in `get_accepted_idx()`.\n   275\t    /// Useful, alongside `get_accepted_idx()`, for observing every entry that\n   276\t    /// enters this node's log -- including ones added by internal protocol\n   277\t    /// handling (e.g. a forwarded proposal or replicated entries) rather than\n   278\t    /// a direct call to `append`/`reconfigure`.\n   279\t    pub fn get_batched_len(&self) -> usize {\n   280\t        self.seq_paxos.internal_storage.get_batched_len()\n   281\t    }\n   282\t\n   283\t    /// Return trim index from storage.\n   284\t    pub fn get_compacted_idx(&self) -> usize {\n   285\t        self.seq_paxos.get_compacted_idx()\n   286\t    }\n   287\t\n   288\t    /// Returns the ID of the current leader and whether the node's `Phase` is `Phase::Accepted`.\n   289\t    ///\n   290\t    /// If the node's phase is `Phase::Accepted`, this implies that the returned leader is also\n   291\t    /// in the accepted phase. However, a `Phase::Prepare` or a `false` response does not\n   292\t    /// necessarily imply that the leader is not in the accepted phase; it only reflects the current\n   293\t    /// phase of this node.\n   294\t    pub fn get_current_leader(&self) -> Option<(NodeId, bool)> {\n   295\t        let promised_pid = self.seq_paxos.get_promise().pid;\n   296\t        if promised_pid == 0 {\n   297\t            None\n   298\t        } else {\n   299\t            let is_accepted = self.seq_paxos.get_state().1 == Phase::Accept;\n   300\t            Some((promised_pid, is_accepted))\n   301\t        }\n   302\t    }\n   303\t\n   304\t    /// Returns the promised ballot of this node.\n   305\t    pub fn get_promise(&self) -> Ballot {\n   306\t        self.seq_paxos.get_promise()\n   307\t    }\n   308\t\n   309\t    /// Returns this node's own pid.\n   310\t    pub fn get_pid(&self) -> NodeId {\n   311\t        self.seq_paxos.get_pid()\n   312\t    }\n   313\t\n   314\t    /// Moves outgoing messages from this server into the buffer. The messages should then be sent via the network implementation.\n   315\t    pub fn take_outgoing_messages(&mut self, buffer: &mut Vec<Message<T>>) {\n   316\t        self.seq_paxos.take_outgoing_msgs(buffer);\n   317\t        buffer.extend(self.ble.outgoing_mut().drain(..).map(|b| Message::BLE(b)));\n   318\t    }\n   319\t\n   320\t    /// Read entry at index `idx` in the log. Returns `None` if `idx` is out of bounds.\n   321\t    pub fn read(&self, idx: usize) -> Option<LogEntry<T>> {\n   322\t        match self\n   323\t            .seq_paxos\n   324\t            .internal_storage\n   325\t            .read(idx..idx + 1)\n   326\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read log entries\")\n   327\t        {\n   328\t            Some(mut v) => v.pop(),\n   329\t            None => None,\n   330\t        }\n   331\t    }\n   332\t\n   333\t    /// Read entries in the range `r` in the log. Returns `None` if `r` is out of bounds.\n   334\t    pub fn read_entries<R>(&self, r: R) -> Option<Vec<LogEntry<T>>>\n   335\t    where\n   336\t        R: RangeBounds<usize>,\n   337\t    {\n   338\t        self.seq_paxos\n   339\t            .internal_storage\n   340\t            .read(r)\n   341\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read log entries\")\n   342\t    }\n   343\t\n   344\t    /// Read all decided entries starting at `from_idx` (inclusive) in the log. Returns `None` if `from_idx` is out of bounds.\n   345\t    pub fn read_decided_suffix(&self, from_idx: usize) -> Option<Vec<LogEntry<T>>> {\n   346\t        self.seq_paxos\n   347\t            .internal_storage\n   348\t            .read_decided_suffix(from_idx)\n   349\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read decided log suffix\")\n   350\t    }\n   351\t\n   352\t    /// Handle an incoming message\n   353\t    pub fn handle_incoming(&mut self, m: Message<T>) {\n   354\t        match m {\n   355\t            Message::SequencePaxos(p) => self.seq_paxos.handle(p),\n   356\t            Message::BLE(b) => self.ble.handle(b),\n   357\t            #[cfg(feature = \"async_runtime\")]\n   358\t            Message::AsyncRuntime(_) => {\n   359\t                // Runtime-layer messages are consumed by the actor before reaching here.\n   360\t                // If one leaks through (e.g. user hand-delivered), silently ignore.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/ballot_leader_election.rs | sed -n '1,300p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/omni_paxos.rs | sed -n '360,510p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/ballot_leader_election.rs | sed -n '1,300p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/omni_paxos.rs | sed -n '360,510p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tuse std::cmp::Ordering;\n     2\t\n     3\t/// Ballot Leader Election algorithm for electing new leaders\n     4\tuse crate::{\n     5\t    sequence_paxos::{Phase, Role},\n     6\t    util::{defaults::*, ConfigurationId, FlexibleQuorum, Quorum},\n     7\t};\n     8\t\n     9\t#[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    10\tuse crate::utils::logger::create_logger;\n    11\tuse crate::{\n    12\t    messages::ballot_leader_election::{\n    13\t        BLEMessage, HeartbeatMsg, HeartbeatReply, HeartbeatRequest,\n    14\t    },\n    15\t    util::NodeId,\n    16\t    OmniPaxosConfig,\n    17\t};\n    18\t#[cfg(feature = \"serde\")]\n    19\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n    20\t#[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    21\tuse slog::{info, trace, Logger};\n    22\t\n    23\t/// Used to define a Sequence Paxos epoch\n    24\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Eq, Debug, Default, PartialEq)]\n    25\t#[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n    26\tpub struct Ballot {\n    27\t    /// The identifier for the configuration that the replica with this ballot is part of.\n    28\t    pub config_id: ConfigurationId,\n    29\t    /// Ballot number\n    30\t    pub n: u32,\n    31\t    /// Custom priority parameter\n    32\t    pub priority: u32,\n    33\t    /// The pid of the process\n    34\t    pub pid: NodeId,\n    35\t}\n    36\t\n    37\timpl Ballot {\n    38\t    /// Creates a new Ballot\n    39\t    /// # Arguments\n    40\t    /// * `config_id` - The identifier for the configuration that the replica with this ballot is part of.\n    41\t    /// * `n` - Ballot number.\n    42\t    /// * `pid` -  Used as tiebreaker for total ordering of ballots.\n    43\t    pub fn with(config_id: ConfigurationId, n: u32, priority: u32, pid: NodeId) -> Ballot {\n    44\t        Ballot {\n    45\t            config_id,\n    46\t            n,\n    47\t            priority,\n    48\t            pid,\n    49\t        }\n    50\t    }\n    51\t}\n    52\t\n    53\timpl Ord for Ballot {\n    54\t    fn cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Ordering {\n    55\t        (self.n, self.priority, self.pid).cmp(&(other.n, other.priority, other.pid))\n    56\t    }\n    57\t}\n    58\t\n    59\timpl PartialOrd for Ballot {\n    60\t    fn partial_cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Option<Ordering> {\n    61\t        Some(self.cmp(other))\n    62\t    }\n    63\t}\n    64\t\n    65\tconst INITIAL_ROUND: u32 = 1;\n    66\tconst RECOVERY_ROUND: u32 = 0;\n    67\t\n    68\t/// A Ballot Leader Election component. Used in conjunction with OmniPaxos to handle the election of a leader for a cluster of OmniPaxos servers,\n    69\t/// incoming messages and produces outgoing messages that the user has to fetch periodically and send using a network implementation.\n    70\t/// User also has to periodically fetch the decided entries that are guaranteed to be strongly consistent and linearizable, and therefore also safe to be used in the higher level application.\n    71\tpub(crate) struct BallotLeaderElection {\n    72\t    /// The identifier for the configuration that this instance is part of.\n    73\t    configuration_id: ConfigurationId,\n    74\t    /// Process identifier used to uniquely identify this instance.\n    75\t    pid: NodeId,\n    76\t    /// Vector that holds the pids of all the other servers.\n    77\t    peers: Vec<NodeId>,\n    78\t    /// The current round of the heartbeat cycle.\n    79\t    hb_round: u32,\n    80\t    /// The heartbeat replies this instance received during the current round.\n    81\t    heartbeat_replies: Vec<HeartbeatReply>,\n    82\t    /// Vector that holds all the received heartbeats from the previous heartbeat round, including the current node. Only used to display the connectivity of this node in the UI.\n    83\t    /// Represents nodes that are currently alive from the view of the current node.\n    84\t    prev_replies: Vec<HeartbeatReply>,\n    85\t    /// Holds the current ballot of this instance.\n    86\t    current_ballot: Ballot,\n    87\t    /// The current leader of this instance.\n    88\t    leader: Ballot,\n    89\t    /// A happy node either sees that it is, is connected to, or sees evidence of a potential leader\n    90\t    /// for the cluster. If a node is unhappy then it is seeking a new leader.\n    91\t    happy: bool,\n    92\t    /// The number of replicas inside the cluster whose heartbeats are needed to become and remain the leader.\n    93\t    quorum: Quorum,\n    94\t    /// Vector which holds all the outgoing messages of the BLE instance.\n    95\t    outgoing: Vec<BLEMessage>,\n    96\t    /// Logger used to output the status of the component.\n    97\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    98\t    logger: Logger,\n    99\t}\n   100\t\n   101\timpl BallotLeaderElection {\n   102\t    /// Construct a new BallotLeaderElection node\n   103\t    pub(crate) fn with(config: BLEConfig, recovered_leader: Option<Ballot>) -> Self {\n   104\t        let config_id = config.configuration_id;\n   105\t        let pid = config.pid;\n   106\t        let peers = config.peers;\n   107\t        let num_nodes = &peers.len() + 1;\n   108\t        let quorum = Quorum::with(config.flexible_quorum, num_nodes);\n   109\t        let mut initial_ballot = Ballot::with(config_id, INITIAL_ROUND, config.priority, pid);\n   110\t        let initial_leader = match recovered_leader {\n   111\t            Some(b) if b != Ballot::default() => {\n   112\t                // Prevents a recovered server from retaining BLE leadership with the same ballot.\n   113\t                initial_ballot.n = RECOVERY_ROUND;\n   114\t                b\n   115\t            }\n   116\t            _ => initial_ballot,\n   117\t        };\n   118\t        let mut ble = BallotLeaderElection {\n   119\t            configuration_id: config_id,\n   120\t            pid,\n   121\t            peers,\n   122\t            hb_round: 0,\n   123\t            heartbeat_replies: Vec::with_capacity(num_nodes),\n   124\t            prev_replies: Vec::with_capacity(num_nodes),\n   125\t            current_ballot: initial_ballot,\n   126\t            leader: initial_leader,\n   127\t            happy: true,\n   128\t            quorum,\n   129\t            outgoing: Vec::with_capacity(config.buffer_size),\n   130\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   131\t            logger: {\n   132\t                if let Some(logger) = config.custom_logger {\n   133\t                    logger\n   134\t                } else {\n   135\t                    let s = config\n   136\t                        .logger_file_path\n   137\t                        .unwrap_or_else(|| format!(\"logs/paxos_{}.log\", pid));\n   138\t                    create_logger(s.as_str())\n   139\t                }\n   140\t            },\n   141\t        };\n   142\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   143\t        {\n   144\t            info!(\n   145\t                ble.logger,\n   146\t                \"Ballot Leader Election component pid: {} created!\", pid\n   147\t            );\n   148\t        }\n   149\t        ble.new_hb_round();\n   150\t        ble\n   151\t    }\n   152\t\n   153\t    /// Update the custom priority used in the Ballot for this server. Note that changing the\n   154\t    /// priority triggers a leader re-election.\n   155\t    pub(crate) fn set_priority(&mut self, p: u32) {\n   156\t        self.current_ballot.priority = p;\n   157\t    }\n   158\t\n   159\t    /// Returns reference to outgoing messages\n   160\t    pub(crate) fn outgoing_mut(&mut self) -> &mut Vec<BLEMessage> {\n   161\t        &mut self.outgoing\n   162\t    }\n   163\t\n   164\t    /// Handle an incoming message.\n   165\t    /// # Arguments\n   166\t    /// * `m` - the message to be handled.\n   167\t    pub(crate) fn handle(&mut self, m: BLEMessage) {\n   168\t        match m.msg {\n   169\t            HeartbeatMsg::Request(req) => self.handle_request(m.from, req),\n   170\t            HeartbeatMsg::Reply(rep) => self.handle_reply(rep),\n   171\t        }\n   172\t    }\n   173\t\n   174\t    /// Initiates a new heartbeat round.\n   175\t    pub(crate) fn new_hb_round(&mut self) {\n   176\t        self.prev_replies = std::mem::take(&mut self.heartbeat_replies);\n   177\t        self.hb_round += 1;\n   178\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   179\t        trace!(\n   180\t            self.logger,\n   181\t            \"Initiate new heartbeat round: {}\",\n   182\t            self.hb_round\n   183\t        );\n   184\t        for peer in &self.peers {\n   185\t            let hb_request = HeartbeatRequest {\n   186\t                round: self.hb_round,\n   187\t            };\n   188\t            self.outgoing.push(BLEMessage {\n   189\t                from: self.pid,\n   190\t                to: *peer,\n   191\t                msg: HeartbeatMsg::Request(hb_request),\n   192\t            });\n   193\t        }\n   194\t    }\n   195\t\n   196\t    /// End of a heartbeat round. Returns current leader and election status.\n   197\t    pub(crate) fn hb_timeout(\n   198\t        &mut self,\n   199\t        seq_paxos_state: &(Role, Phase),\n   200\t        seq_paxos_promise: Ballot,\n   201\t    ) -> Option<Ballot> {\n   202\t        self.update_leader();\n   203\t        self.update_happiness(seq_paxos_state);\n   204\t        self.check_takeover();\n   205\t        self.new_hb_round();\n   206\t        if seq_paxos_promise > self.leader {\n   207\t            // Sync leader with Paxos promise in case ballot didn't make it to BLE followers\n   208\t            // or become_leader() was called.\n   209\t            self.leader = seq_paxos_promise;\n   210\t            if seq_paxos_promise.pid == self.pid {\n   211\t                self.current_ballot = seq_paxos_promise;\n   212\t            }\n   213\t            self.happy = true;\n   214\t        }\n   215\t        if self.leader == self.current_ballot {\n   216\t            Some(self.current_ballot)\n   217\t        } else {\n   218\t            None\n   219\t        }\n   220\t    }\n   221\t\n   222\t    fn update_leader(&mut self) {\n   223\t        let max_reply_ballot = self.heartbeat_replies.iter().map(|r| r.ballot).max();\n   224\t        if let Some(max) = max_reply_ballot {\n   225\t            if max > self.leader {\n   226\t                self.leader = max;\n   227\t            }\n   228\t        }\n   229\t    }\n   230\t\n   231\t    fn update_happiness(&mut self, seq_paxos_state: &(Role, Phase)) {\n   232\t        self.happy = if self.leader == self.current_ballot {\n   233\t            let potential_followers = self\n   234\t                .heartbeat_replies\n   235\t                .iter()\n   236\t                .filter(|hb_reply| hb_reply.leader <= self.current_ballot)\n   237\t                .count();\n   238\t            let can_form_quorum = match seq_paxos_state {\n   239\t                (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) => {\n   240\t                    self.quorum.is_accept_quorum(potential_followers + 1)\n   241\t                }\n   242\t                _ => self.quorum.is_prepare_quorum(potential_followers + 1),\n   243\t            };\n   244\t            if can_form_quorum {\n   245\t                true\n   246\t            } else {\n   247\t                let see_larger_happy_leader = self\n   248\t                    .heartbeat_replies\n   249\t                    .iter()\n   250\t                    .any(|r| r.leader > self.current_ballot && r.happy);\n   251\t                see_larger_happy_leader\n   252\t            }\n   253\t        } else {\n   254\t            self.heartbeat_replies\n   255\t                .iter()\n   256\t                .any(|r| r.ballot == self.leader && r.happy)\n   257\t        };\n   258\t    }\n   259\t\n   260\t    fn check_takeover(&mut self) {\n   261\t        if !self.happy {\n   262\t            let all_neighbors_unhappy = self.heartbeat_replies.iter().all(|r| !r.happy);\n   263\t            let im_quorum_connected = self\n   264\t                .quorum\n   265\t                .is_prepare_quorum(self.heartbeat_replies.len() + 1);\n   266\t            if all_neighbors_unhappy && im_quorum_connected {\n   267\t                // We increment past our leader instead of max of unhappy ballots because we\n   268\t                // assume we have already checked leader for this round so they should be equal\n   269\t                self.current_ballot.n = self.leader.n + 1;\n   270\t                self.leader = self.current_ballot;\n   271\t                self.happy = true;\n   272\t            }\n   273\t        }\n   274\t    }\n   275\t\n   276\t    fn handle_request(&mut self, from: NodeId, req: HeartbeatRequest) {\n   277\t        let hb_reply = HeartbeatReply {\n   278\t            round: req.round,\n   279\t            ballot: self.current_ballot,\n   280\t            leader: self.leader,\n   281\t            happy: self.happy,\n   282\t        };\n   283\t        self.outgoing.push(BLEMessage {\n   284\t            from: self.pid,\n   285\t            to: from,\n   286\t            msg: HeartbeatMsg::Reply(hb_reply),\n   287\t        });\n   288\t    }\n   289\t\n   290\t    fn handle_reply(&mut self, rep: HeartbeatReply) {\n   291\t        if rep.round == self.hb_round && rep.ballot.config_id == self.configuration_id {\n   292\t            self.heartbeat_replies.push(rep);\n   293\t        }\n   294\t    }\n   295\t\n   296\t    pub(crate) fn get_current_ballot(&self) -> Ballot {\n   297\t        self.current_ballot\n   298\t    }\n   299\t\n   300\t    pub(crate) fn get_ballots(&self) -> Vec<HeartbeatReply> {\n   360\t                // If one leaks through (e.g. user hand-delivered), silently ignore.\n   361\t            }\n   362\t        }\n   363\t    }\n   364\t\n   365\t    /// Returns whether this Sequence Paxos has been reconfigured\n   366\t    pub fn is_reconfigured(&self) -> Option<StopSign> {\n   367\t        self.seq_paxos.is_reconfigured()\n   368\t    }\n   369\t\n   370\t    /// Append an entry to the replicated log.\n   371\t    pub fn append(&mut self, entry: T) -> Result<(), ProposeErr<T>> {\n   372\t        self.seq_paxos.append(entry)\n   373\t    }\n   374\t\n   375\t    /// Propose a cluster reconfiguration. Returns an error if the current configuration has already been stopped\n   376\t    /// by a previous reconfiguration request or if the `new_configuration` is invalid.\n   377\t    /// `new_configuration` defines the cluster-wide configuration settings for the **next** cluster.\n   378\t    /// `metadata` is optional data to commit alongside the reconfiguration.\n   379\t    pub fn reconfigure(\n   380\t        &mut self,\n   381\t        new_configuration: ClusterConfig,\n   382\t        metadata: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n   383\t    ) -> Result<(), ProposeErr<T>> {\n   384\t        if let Err(config_error) = new_configuration.validate() {\n   385\t            return Err(ProposeErr::ConfigError(\n   386\t                config_error,\n   387\t                new_configuration,\n   388\t                metadata,\n   389\t            ));\n   390\t        }\n   391\t        self.seq_paxos.reconfigure(new_configuration, metadata)\n   392\t    }\n   393\t\n   394\t    /// Handles re-establishing a connection to a previously disconnected peer.\n   395\t    /// This should only be called if the underlying network implementation indicates that a connection has been re-established.\n   396\t    pub fn reconnected(&mut self, pid: NodeId) {\n   397\t        self.seq_paxos.reconnected(pid)\n   398\t    }\n   399\t\n   400\t    /// Increments the internal logical clock. This drives the processes for leader changes, resending dropped messages, and flushing batched log entries.\n   401\t    /// Each of these is triggered every `election_tick_timeout`, `resend_message_tick_timeout`, and `flush_batch_tick_timeout` number of calls to this function\n   402\t    /// (See how to configure these timeouts in `ServerConfig`).\n   403\t    pub fn tick(&mut self) {\n   404\t        if self.election_clock.tick_and_check_timeout() {\n   405\t            self.election_timeout();\n   406\t        }\n   407\t        if self.resend_message_clock.tick_and_check_timeout() {\n   408\t            self.seq_paxos.resend_message_timeout();\n   409\t        }\n   410\t        if self.flush_batch_clock.tick_and_check_timeout() {\n   411\t            self.seq_paxos.flush_batch_timeout();\n   412\t        }\n   413\t    }\n   414\t\n   415\t    /// Manually attempt to become the leader by incrementing this instance's Ballot. Calling this\n   416\t    /// function may not result in gainig leadership if other instances are competing for\n   417\t    /// leadership with higher Ballots.\n   418\t    pub fn try_become_leader(&mut self) {\n   419\t        let mut my_ballot = self.ble.get_current_ballot();\n   420\t        let promise = self.seq_paxos.get_promise();\n   421\t        my_ballot.n = promise.n + 1;\n   422\t        self.seq_paxos.handle_leader(my_ballot);\n   423\t    }\n   424\t\n   425\t    /*** BLE calls ***/\n   426\t    /// Update the custom priority used in the Ballot for this server. Note that changing the\n   427\t    /// priority triggers a leader re-election.\n   428\t    pub fn set_priority(&mut self, p: u32) {\n   429\t        self.ble.set_priority(p)\n   430\t    }\n   431\t\n   432\t    /// If the heartbeat of a leader is not received when election_timeout() is called, the server might attempt to become the leader.\n   433\t    /// It is also used for the election process, where the server checks if it can become the leader.\n   434\t    /// For instance if `election_timeout()` is called every 100ms, then if the leader fails, the servers will detect it after 100ms and elect a new server after another 100ms if possible.\n   435\t    fn election_timeout(&mut self) {\n   436\t        if let Some(new_leader) = self\n   437\t            .ble\n   438\t            .hb_timeout(self.seq_paxos.get_state(), self.seq_paxos.get_promise())\n   439\t        {\n   440\t            self.seq_paxos.handle_leader(new_leader);\n   441\t        }\n   442\t    }\n   443\t\n   444\t    /// Returns the current states of the OmniPaxos instance for OmniPaxos UI to display.\n   445\t    pub fn get_ui_states(&self) -> ui::OmniPaxosStates {\n   446\t        let mut cluster_state = ClusterState::from(self.seq_paxos.get_leader_state());\n   447\t        cluster_state.heartbeats = self.ble.get_ballots();\n   448\t\n   449\t        ui::OmniPaxosStates {\n   450\t            current_ballot: self.ble.get_current_ballot(),\n   451\t            current_leader: self.get_current_leader().map(|(leader, _)| leader),\n   452\t            decided_idx: self.get_decided_idx(),\n   453\t            heartbeats: self.ble.get_ballots(),\n   454\t            cluster_state,\n   455\t        }\n   456\t    }\n   457\t}\n   458\t\n   459\t/// An error indicating a failed proposal due to the current cluster configuration being already stopped\n   460\t/// or due to an invalid proposed configuration. Returns the failed proposal.\n   461\t#[derive(Debug)]\n   462\tpub enum ProposeErr<T>\n   463\twhere\n   464\t    T: Entry,\n   465\t{\n   466\t    /// Couldn't propose entry because a reconfiguration is pending. Returns the failed, proposed entry.\n   467\t    PendingReconfigEntry(T),\n   468\t    /// Couldn't propose reconfiguration because a reconfiguration is already pending. Returns the failed, proposed `ClusterConfig` and the metadata.\n   469\t    /// cluster config and metadata.\n   470\t    PendingReconfigConfig(ClusterConfig, Option<Vec<u8>>),\n   471\t    /// Couldn't propose reconfiguration because of an invalid cluster config. Contains the config\n   472\t    /// error and the failed, proposed cluster config and metadata.\n   473\t    ConfigError(ConfigError, ClusterConfig, Option<Vec<u8>>),\n   474\t}\n   475\t\n   476\t/// An error returning the proposal that was failed due to that the current configuration is stopped.\n   477\t#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug)]\n   478\tpub enum CompactionErr {\n   479\t    /// Snapshot was called with an index that is not decided yet. Returns the currently decided index.\n   480\t    UndecidedIndex(usize),\n   481\t    /// Snapshot was called with an index which is already trimmed. Returns the currently compacted index.\n   482\t    TrimmedIndex(usize),\n   483\t    /// Trim was called with an index that is not decided by all servers yet. Returns the index decided by ALL servers currently.\n   484\t    NotAllDecided(usize),\n   485\t    /// Trim was called at a follower node. Trim must be called by the leader, which is the returned NodeId.\n   486\t    NotCurrentLeader(NodeId),\n   487\t}\n   488\t\n   489\timpl Error for CompactionErr {}\n   490\timpl Display for CompactionErr {\n   491\t    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {\n   492\t        Debug::fmt(self, f)\n   493\t    }\n   494\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/communication.md ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/reconfiguration.md ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/storage.md; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/communication.md ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/reconfiguration.md ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/storage.md; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"As previously mentioned, the user has to send/receive messages between servers themselves. In this section, we show how the user should interact with `OmniPaxos` and its incoming and outgoing messages.\n\n## Incoming and Outgoing\nWhen a message is received from the network layer intended for our node, we need to handle it in `OmniPaxos`.\n\n```rust\nuse omnipaxos::messages::Message;\n\n// handle incoming message from network layer\nlet msg: Message<KeyValue> = in_msg;    // in_msg is a received message for this node e.g. `in_msg.get_receiver() == 2`\nomni_paxos.handle_incoming(msg);\n```\n\nBy handling incoming messages and local calls such as `append()`, our local `omni_paxos` will produce outgoing messages for its peers. Thus, we must periodically send the outgoing messages on the network layer.\n\n```rust\n// send outgoing messages. This should be called periodically, e.g. every ms\nlet mut msg_buffer = Vec::with_capacity(1000);\nomni_paxos.take_outgoing_messages(&mut msg_buffer);\nfor out_msg in msg_buffer.drain(..) {\n    let receiver = out_msg.get_receiver();\n    // send out_msg to receiver on network layer\n}\n```\n\n> **Note:** The networking i.e. how to actually send and receive messages needs to be implemented by you, the user. You have to periodically fetch these outgoing messages from `OmniPaxos`.\nTo change the servers in the cluster, we must first stop the current OmniPaxos cluster. This is done via the `reconfigure()` function, which takes a `ClusterConfig` that contains the settings for the next OmniPaxos cluster and some optional metadata.\n\n```rust\n// Node 3 seems to have crashed... let's replace it with a new node 4.\nlet new_configuration = ClusterConfig {\n    configuration_id: 2,\n    nodes: vec![1, 2, 4],\n    ..Default::default()\n};\nlet metadata = None;\nomni_paxos.reconfigure(new_configuration, metadata).expect(\"Failed to propose reconfiguration\");\n```\n\nCalling ``reconfigure()`` will propose a `StopSign` entry to be appended. If it gets decided, the log is sealed and prevented from being further appended. From the `StopSign` entry, all nodes will be able to see the new configuration. When you, the user, read from a node and find a `LogEntry::StopSign` in the log, you should start a new `OmniPaxos` instance at this node if it is part of the new configuration.\n\n```rust\n    // the ServerConfig config for current node\n    let current_config = ServerConfig {\n        pid: 2,\n        ..Default::default()\n    };\n    let my_pid = current_config.pid;\n    \n    let idx: usize = 2;  // some index we last read from\n    let decided_entries: Option<Vec<LogEntry<KeyValue>>> = omni_paxos.read_decided_suffix(idx);\n\n    if let Some(de) = decided_entries {\n        for d in de {\n            match d {\n                LogEntry::StopSign(stopsign, true) => {\n                    let new_configuration = stopsign.next_config;\n                    if new_configuration.nodes.contains(&my_pid) {\n                        // current configuration has been safely stopped. Start new instance\n                        let new_storage = MemoryStorage::default();\n                        let mut new_omnipaxos = new_configuration.build_for_server(current_config.clone(), MemoryStorage::default()).unwrap();\n\n                        // use new_omnipaxos\n                        // ...\n                    }\n                }\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n```\n\n> **Note:** New nodes will not see the `StopSign` since they were not part of the old configuration. The user themselves must notify and start these new nodes. Furthermore,the user must ensure these new nodes have the application state or log up to the stopsign before starting their `OmniPaxos` instance.\nYou are free to use any storage implementation with `OmniPaxos`. The only requirement is that it implements the `Storage` trait. OmniPaxos includes the package `omnipaxos_storage` which provides two types of storage implementation that work out of the box: `MemoryStorage` and `PersistentStorage`.\n\n## Importing `omnipaxos_storage`\nTo use the provided storage implementations, we need to add `omnipaxos_storage` to the dependencies in the cargo file. You can find the latest version on [crates](https://crates.io/crates/omnipaxos_storage).\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nomnipaxos_storage = { version = \"LATEST_VERSION\", default-features = true }\n```\n\n**If** you **do** decide to implement your own storage, we recommend taking a look at `MemoryStorage` as a reference for implementing the functions required by `Storage`.\nUpon receiving a `StorageResult::Error(_)` from the storage implementation, Omnipaxos tries to roll back incomplete changes, to enable crash-recovery, and then panicks.\n\n## MemoryStorage\n`MemoryStorage` is an in-memory storage implementation and it will be used in our examples. For simplicity, we leave out some parts of the implementation for now (such as [Snapshots](../compaction)).\n```rust\n// from the module omnipaxos_storage::memory_storage\n#[derive(Clone)]\npub struct MemoryStorage<T>\nwhere\n    T: Entry,\n{\n    /// Vector which contains all the replicated entries in-memory.\n    log: Vec<T>,\n    /// Last promised round.\n    n_prom: Ballot,\n    /// Last accepted round.\n    acc_round: Ballot,\n    /// Length of the decided log.\n    ld: usize,\n    /// Garbage collected index.\n    trimmed_idx: usize,\n    ...\n}\n\nimpl<T> Storage<T> for MemoryStorage<T>\n    where\n    T: Entry,\n{\n    fn write_atomically(&mut self, ops: Vec<StorageOp<T>>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        for op in ops {\n            match op {\n                StorageOp::AppendEntry(entry) => self.append_entry(entry)?,\n                StorageOp::AppendEntries(entries) => self.append_entries(entries)?,\n                StorageOp::AppendOnPrefix(from_idx, entries) => {\n                    self.append_on_prefix(from_idx, entries)?\n                }\n                StorageOp::SetPromise(bal) => self.set_promise(bal)?,\n                StorageOp::SetDecidedIndex(idx) => self.set_decided_idx(idx)?,\n                StorageOp::SetAcceptedRound(bal) => self.set_accepted_round(bal)?,\n                ...\n            }\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn append_entry(&mut self, entry: T) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        self.log.push(entry);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn append_entries(&mut self, entries: Vec<T>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        let mut e = entries;\n        self.log.append(&mut e);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn append_on_prefix(&mut self, from_idx: usize, entries: Vec<T>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        self.log.truncate(from_idx - self.trimmed_idx);\n        self.append_entries(entries)\n    }\n\n    fn set_promise(&mut self, n_prom: Ballot) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        self.n_prom = Some(n_prom);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn set_decided_idx(&mut self, ld: usize) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        self.ld = ld;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn get_decided_idx(&self) -> StorageResult<usize> {\n        Ok(self.ld)\n    }\n\n    fn set_accepted_round(&mut self, na: Ballot) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        self.acc_round = Some(na);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn get_accepted_round(&self) -> StorageResult<Option<Ballot>> {\n        Ok(self.acc_round)\n    }\n\n    fn get_entries(&self, from: usize, to: usize) -> StorageResult<Vec<T>> {\n        let from = from - self.trimmed_idx;\n        let to = to - self.trimmed_idx;\n        Ok(self.log.get(from..to).unwrap_or(&[]).to_vec())\n    }\n\n    fn get_log_len(&self) -> StorageResult<usize> {\n        Ok(self.log.len())\n    }\n\n    fn get_suffix(&self, from: usize) -> StorageResult<Vec<T>> {\n        Ok(match self.log.get((from - self.trimmed_idx)..) {\n                Some(s) => s.to_vec(),\n                None => vec![],\n                })\n    }\n\n    fn get_promise(&self) -> StorageResult<Option<Ballot>> {\n        Ok(self.n_prom)\n    }\n\n    fn trim(&mut self, trimmed_idx: usize) -> StorageResult<()> {\n        let to_trim = (trimmed_idx - self.trimmed_idx).min(self.log.len());\n        self.log.drain(0..to_trim);\n        self.trimmed_idx = trimmed_idx;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n    ...\n    }\n```\n\n## PersistentStorage\n`PersistentStorage` is a persistent storage implementation, built on top of [RocksDB](https://crates.io/crates/rocksdb), that stores the replicated log and the state of OmniPaxos. It can be enabled with the \"persistent_storage\" feature flag. Users can configure the path to log entries and OmniPaxos state, and storage-related options through `PersistentStorageConfig`. The configuration struct features a `default()` constructor for generating default configuration, and the constructor `with()` that takes the storage path and options as arguments.\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nomnipaxos_storage = { version = \"LATEST_VERSION\", features=[\"persistent_storage\"] }\n```\nThe persistent storage implementation must first be enabled via the \"persistent_storage\" feature flag.\n\n```rust\nuse omnipaxos_storage::{\n    persistent_storage::{PersistentStorage, PersistentStorageConfig},\n};\nuse rocksdb;\n\n// user-defined configuration\nlet my_path = \"my_storage\";\nlet log_store_options = rocksdb::Options::default();\nlet state_store_options = rocksdb::Options::default();\nstate_store_options.create_missing_column_families(true); // required\nstate_store_options.create_if_missing(true); // required\n\n// generate default configuration and set user-defined options\nlet mut my_config = PersistentStorageConfig::default();\nmy_config.set_path(my_path.to_string());\nmy_config.set_database_options(state_store_options);\nmy_config.set_log_options(log_store_options);\n```\n## Batching\nOmniPaxos supports batching to reduce the number of IO operations to storage. It is enabled by specifying the `batch_size` in `OmniPaxosConfig`.\n\n```rust\n    let omnipaxos_config = OmniPaxosConfig {\n        server_config: ServerConfig {\n            batch_size: 100, // `batch_size = 1` by default\n            ..Default::default()\n        },\n        cluster_config: ClusterConfig {\n            configuration_id: 1,\n            nodes: vec![1, 2, 3],\n            ..Default::default()\n        },\n    };\n    // build omnipaxos instance\n```\n\n> **Note** OmniPaxos will wait until the batch size is reached before the entries get decided. A larger batch size may therefore incur higher latency before an append operation is decided. \n     1\tuse super::state_cache::StateCache;\n     2\tuse crate::{\n     3\t    ballot_leader_election::Ballot,\n     4\t    storage::{Entry, Snapshot, SnapshotType, StopSign, Storage, StorageOp, StorageResult},\n     5\t    util::{AcceptedMetaData, IndexEntry, LogEntry, LogSync, SnapshottedEntry},\n     6\t    CompactionErr,\n     7\t};\n     8\t#[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n     9\tuse crate::{unicache::*, util::NodeId};\n    10\tuse std::{\n    11\t    cmp::Ordering,\n    12\t    marker::PhantomData,\n    13\t    ops::{Bound, RangeBounds},\n    14\t};\n    15\t\n    16\tpub(crate) struct InternalStorageConfig {\n    17\t    pub(crate) batch_size: usize,\n    18\t}\n    19\t\n    20\t/// Internal representation of storage. Serves as the interface between Sequence Paxos and the\n    21\t/// storage back-end.\n    22\tpub(crate) struct InternalStorage<I, T>\n    23\twhere\n    24\t    I: Storage<T>,\n    25\t    T: Entry,\n    26\t{\n    27\t    storage: I,\n    28\t    state_cache: StateCache<T>,\n    29\t    _t: PhantomData<T>,\n    30\t}\n    31\t\n    32\timpl<I, T> InternalStorage<I, T>\n    33\twhere\n    34\t    I: Storage<T>,\n    35\t    T: Entry,\n    36\t{\n    37\t    pub(crate) fn with(\n    38\t        storage: I,\n    39\t        config: InternalStorageConfig,\n    40\t        #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")] pid: NodeId,\n    41\t    ) -> Self {\n    42\t        let mut internal_store = InternalStorage {\n    43\t            storage,\n    44\t            state_cache: StateCache::new(\n    45\t                config,\n    46\t                #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    47\t                pid,\n    48\t            ),\n    49\t            _t: Default::default(),\n    50\t        };\n    51\t        internal_store.load_cache();\n    52\t        internal_store\n    53\t    }\n    54\t\n    55\t    fn load_cache(&mut self) {\n    56\t        self.state_cache.promise = self\n    57\t            .storage\n    58\t            .get_promise()\n    59\t            .expect(\"Failed to load cache from storage.\")\n    60\t            .unwrap_or_default();\n    61\t        self.state_cache.decided_idx = self.storage.get_decided_idx().unwrap();\n    62\t        self.state_cache.accepted_round = self\n    63\t            .storage\n    64\t            .get_accepted_round()\n    65\t            .unwrap()\n    66\t            .unwrap_or_default();\n    67\t        self.state_cache.compacted_idx = self.storage.get_compacted_idx().unwrap();\n    68\t        self.state_cache.stopsign = self.storage.get_stopsign().unwrap();\n    69\t        self.state_cache.accepted_idx =\n    70\t            self.storage.get_log_len().unwrap() + self.state_cache.compacted_idx;\n    71\t        if self.state_cache.stopsign.is_some() {\n    72\t            self.state_cache.accepted_idx += 1;\n    73\t        }\n    74\t    }\n    75\t\n    76\t    /// Read all decided entries from `from_idx` in the log. Returns `None` if `from_idx` is out of bounds.\n    77\t    pub(crate) fn read_decided_suffix(\n    78\t        &self,\n    79\t        from_idx: usize,\n    80\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<Vec<LogEntry<T>>>> {\n    81\t        let decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx();\n    82\t        if from_idx < decided_idx {\n    83\t            self.read(from_idx..decided_idx)\n    84\t        } else {\n    85\t            Ok(None)\n    86\t        }\n    87\t    }\n    88\t\n    89\t    /// Read entries in the range `r` in the log. Returns `None` if `r` is out of bounds.\n    90\t    pub(crate) fn read<R>(&self, r: R) -> StorageResult<Option<Vec<LogEntry<T>>>>\n    91\t    where\n    92\t        R: RangeBounds<usize>,\n    93\t    {\n    94\t        let from_idx = match r.start_bound() {\n    95\t            Bound::Included(i) => *i,\n    96\t            Bound::Excluded(e) => *e + 1,\n    97\t            Bound::Unbounded => 0,\n    98\t        };\n    99\t        let to_idx = match r.end_bound() {\n   100\t            Bound::Included(i) => *i + 1,\n   101\t            Bound::Excluded(e) => *e,\n   102\t            Bound::Unbounded => self.get_accepted_idx(),\n   103\t        };\n   104\t        if to_idx == 0 {\n   105\t            return Ok(None);\n   106\t        }\n   107\t        let compacted_idx = self.get_compacted_idx();\n   108\t        let accepted_idx = self.get_accepted_idx();\n   109\t        // use to_idx-1 when getting the entry type as to_idx is exclusive\n   110\t        let to_type = match self.get_entry_type(to_idx - 1, compacted_idx, accepted_idx)? {\n   111\t            Some(IndexEntry::Compacted) => {\n   112\t                return Ok(Some(vec![self.create_compacted_entry(compacted_idx)?]))\n   113\t            }\n   114\t            Some(from_type) => from_type,\n   115\t            _ => return Ok(None),\n   116\t        };\n   117\t        let from_type = match self.get_entry_type(from_idx, compacted_idx, accepted_idx)? {\n   118\t            Some(from_type) => from_type,\n   119\t            _ => return Ok(None),\n   120\t        };\n   121\t        match (from_type, to_type) {\n   122\t            (IndexEntry::Entry, IndexEntry::Entry) => {\n   123\t                Ok(Some(self.create_read_log_entries(from_idx, to_idx)?))\n   124\t            }\n   125\t            (IndexEntry::Entry, IndexEntry::StopSign(ss)) => {\n   126\t                let mut entries = self.create_read_log_entries(from_idx, to_idx - 1)?;\n   127\t                entries.push(LogEntry::StopSign(ss, self.stopsign_is_decided()));\n   128\t                Ok(Some(entries))\n   129\t            }\n   130\t            (IndexEntry::Compacted, IndexEntry::Entry) => {\n   131\t                let mut entries = Vec::with_capacity(to_idx - compacted_idx + 1);\n   132\t                let compacted = self.create_compacted_entry(compacted_idx)?;\n   133\t                entries.push(compacted);\n   134\t                let mut e = self.create_read_log_entries(compacted_idx, to_idx)?;\n   135\t                entries.append(&mut e);\n   136\t                Ok(Some(entries))\n   137\t            }\n   138\t            (IndexEntry::Compacted, IndexEntry::StopSign(ss)) => {\n   139\t                let mut entries = Vec::with_capacity(to_idx - compacted_idx + 1);\n   140\t                let compacted = self.create_compacted_entry(compacted_idx)?;\n   141\t                entries.push(compacted);\n   142\t                let mut e = self.create_read_log_entries(compacted_idx, to_idx - 1)?;\n   143\t                entries.append(&mut e);\n   144\t                entries.push(LogEntry::StopSign(ss, self.stopsign_is_decided()));\n   145\t                Ok(Some(entries))\n   146\t            }\n   147\t            (IndexEntry::StopSign(ss), IndexEntry::StopSign(_)) => {\n   148\t                Ok(Some(vec![LogEntry::StopSign(\n   149\t                    ss,\n   150\t                    self.stopsign_is_decided(),\n   151\t                )]))\n   152\t            }\n   153\t            e => {\n   154\t                unimplemented!(\"{}\", format!(\"Unexpected read combination: {:?}\", e))\n   155\t            }\n   156\t        }\n   157\t    }\n   158\t\n   159\t    fn get_entry_type(\n   160\t        &self,\n   161\t        idx: usize,\n   162\t        compacted_idx: usize,\n   163\t        accepted_idx: usize,\n   164\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<IndexEntry>> {\n   165\t        if idx < compacted_idx {\n   166\t            Ok(Some(IndexEntry::Compacted))\n   167\t        } else if idx + 1 < accepted_idx {\n   168\t            Ok(Some(IndexEntry::Entry))\n   169\t        } else if idx + 1 == accepted_idx {\n   170\t            match self.get_stopsign() {\n   171\t                Some(ss) => Ok(Some(IndexEntry::StopSign(ss))),\n   172\t                _ => Ok(Some(IndexEntry::Entry)),\n   173\t            }\n   174\t        } else {\n   175\t            Ok(None)\n   176\t        }\n   177\t    }\n   178\t\n   179\t    fn create_read_log_entries(&self, from: usize, to: usize) -> StorageResult<Vec<LogEntry<T>>> {\n   180\t        let decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx();\n   181\t        let entries = self\n   182\t            .get_entries(from, to)?\n   183\t            .into_iter()\n   184\t            .enumerate()\n   185\t            .map(|(idx, e)| {\n   186\t                let log_idx = idx + from;\n   187\t                if log_idx < decided_idx {\n   188\t                    LogEntry::Decided(e)\n   189\t                } else {\n   190\t                    LogEntry::Undecided(e)\n   191\t                }\n   192\t            })\n   193\t            .collect();\n   194\t        Ok(entries)\n   195\t    }\n   196\t\n   197\t    fn create_compacted_entry(&self, compacted_idx: usize) -> StorageResult<LogEntry<T>> {\n   198\t        self.storage.get_snapshot().map(|snap| match snap {\n   199\t            Some(s) => LogEntry::Snapshotted(SnapshottedEntry::with(compacted_idx, s)),\n   200\t            None => LogEntry::Trimmed(compacted_idx),\n   201\t        })\n   202\t    }\n   203\t\n   204\t    // Append entry, if the batch size is reached, flush the batch and return the actual\n   205\t    // accepted index (not including the batched entries)\n   206\t    pub(crate) fn append_entry_with_batching(\n   207\t        &mut self,\n   208\t        entry: T,\n   209\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<AcceptedMetaData<T>>> {\n   210\t        let append_res = self.state_cache.append_entry(entry);\n   211\t        self.flush_if_full_batch(append_res)\n   212\t    }\n   213\t\n   214\t    // Append entries in batch, if the batch size is reached, flush the batch and return the\n   215\t    // accepted index and the flushed entries. If the batch size is not reached, return None.\n   216\t    pub(crate) fn append_entries_with_batching(\n   217\t        &mut self,\n   218\t        entries: Vec<T>,\n   219\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<AcceptedMetaData<T>>> {\n   220\t        let append_res = self.state_cache.append_entries(entries);\n   221\t        self.flush_if_full_batch(append_res)\n   222\t    }\n   223\t\n   224\t    // Flushes batched entries and appends a stopsign to the log. Returns the AcceptedMetaData\n   225\t    // associated with any flushed entries if there were any.\n   226\t    pub(crate) fn append_stopsign(\n   227\t        &mut self,\n   228\t        ss: StopSign,\n   229\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<AcceptedMetaData<T>>> {\n   230\t        let append_res = self.state_cache.append_stopsign(ss.clone());\n   231\t        let accepted_entries_metadata = self.flush_if_full_batch(append_res)?;\n   232\t        self.storage.set_stopsign(Some(ss))?;\n   233\t        self.state_cache.accepted_idx += 1;\n   234\t        Ok(accepted_entries_metadata)\n   235\t    }\n   236\t\n   237\t    fn flush_if_full_batch(\n   238\t        &mut self,\n   239\t        append_res: Option<Vec<T>>,\n   240\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<AcceptedMetaData<T>>> {\n   241\t        if let Some(flushed_entries) = append_res {\n   242\t            let accepted_idx = self.append_entries_without_batching(flushed_entries.clone())?;\n   243\t            Ok(Some(AcceptedMetaData {\n   244\t                accepted_idx,\n   245\t                #[cfg(not(feature = \"unicache\"))]\n   246\t                entries: flushed_entries,\n   247\t                #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n   248\t                entries: self.state_cache.take_batched_processed(),\n   249\t            }))\n   250\t        } else {\n   251\t            Ok(None)\n   252\t        }\n   253\t    }\n   254\t\n   255\t    // Append entries in batch, if the batch size is reached, flush the batch and return the\n   256\t    // accepted index. If the batch size is not reached, return None.\n   257\t    pub(crate) fn append_entries_and_get_accepted_idx(\n   258\t        &mut self,\n   259\t        entries: Vec<T>,\n   260\t    ) -> StorageResult<Option<usize>> {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The normal decision path ties acknowledgments to a leader ballot and counts support by node. On a leader change, the new leader collects promises and adopts the highest accepted history before sending synchronization messages. Recovery resets follower sequencing and uses Prepare/Promise exchange to restore participation.\n\nI’m now checking the boundaries around those protections: configuration identity, recovery history, and how callers observe completion. These remain questions, not findings."}}
